      "hints": [
        "Substitute the Pythagorean identity $\\sin^2\\theta = 1 - \\cos^2\\theta$ into $8\\sin^2\\theta + 6\\cos\\theta + 1 = 0$.",
        "Rearrange into standard quadratic form $8\\cos^2\\theta - 6\\cos\\theta - 9 = 0$.",
        "Factorise $(4\\cos\\theta + 3)(2\\cos\\theta - 3) = 0$ and solve for $\\theta$ in $0^\\circ < \\theta < 180^\\circ$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Use the identity $\\sin^2\\theta = 1 - \\cos^2\\theta$ to write the equation purely in terms of $\\cos\\theta$:\n$$8(1 - \\cos^2\\theta) + 6\\cos\\theta + 1 = 0$$\n$$8 - 8\\cos^2\\theta + 6\\cos\\theta + 1 = 0 \\implies 8\\cos^2\\theta - 6\\cos\\theta - 9 = 0$$",
        "Factorise the quadratic equation in terms of $\\cos\\theta$:\n$$(4\\cos\\theta + 3)(2\\cos\\theta - 3) = 0$$",
        "Solve for $\\cos\\theta$:\n$$\\cos\\theta = -\\frac{3}{4} = -0.75 \\quad \\text{or} \\quad \\cos\\theta = \\frac{3}{2} = 1.5 \\quad (\\text{no real solutions, since } |\\cos\\theta| \\le 1)$$",
        "Find the obtuse angle $\\theta$ in the interval $0^\\circ < \\theta < 180^\\circ$:\n$$\\theta = \\cos^{-1}(-0.75) \\approx 138.6^\\circ$$"
      ],
